{"_defaults": {"l": "hi"}}
{"t": "आवाज़ बढ़ाओ", "i": "volume_up", "n": "Tier 8: Devanagari gap closed - volume_up's contains_phrases now include this literal phrase alongside the pre-existing romanized 'awaaz badhao'."}
{"t": "आवाज़ कम करो", "i": "volume_down", "n": "Tier 8: same fix as above, for volume_down."}
{"t": "म्यूट करो", "i": "mute_volume", "n": "Tier 14: toggle_mute retired, replaced by mute_volume/unmute_volume - this phrase moved to mute_volume's own contains_phrases list."}
{"t": "कंप्यूटर लॉक करो", "i": "lock_pc", "n": "Tier 8: same fix, for lock_pc."}
{"t": "स्क्रीनशॉट लो", "i": "take_screenshot", "n": "Tier 8: same fix, for take_screenshot."}
{"t": "पिछला गाना", "i": "media_previous_track", "n": "Tier 8: media_previous_track had zero phrase in ANY script before this - added both this Devanagari phrase and a romanized 'pichla gaana' variant."}
{"t": "यह पूर्ववत करो", "i": "undo_last_action", "n": "Tier 8: added as a new exact-match phrase alongside the existing romanized ones (undo is an _exact rule, not _contains)."}
{"t": "क्रोम खोलो", "i": "open_app", "a": {"app_name": "क्रोम"}, "n": "Tier 8: open_app now also matches verb-FINAL phrasing via the new _suffix_arg matcher (' खोलो' as a suffix), not just the English verb-first 'open '/'start '/'launch ' prefixes - see _prefix_or_suffix_arg in brain/intent_router.py."}
{"t": "नोटपैड बंद करो", "i": "close_app", "a": {"app_name": "नोटपैड"}, "n": "Tier 8: same verb-final fix as open_app above, for close_app (' बंद करो' as a suffix) - this is also the Devanagari half of the same gap intents_hinglish.jsonl's 'notepad band karo' row documents for the romanized side."}
{"t": "मुझे कल सुबह याद दिलाना डॉक्टर के पास जाना है", "i": "chat", "n": "still out of scope - reminders have no intent_router rule at all, in any script. Not touched in Tier 8; see Readme.MD."}
{"t": "आज जयपुर में मौसम कैसा है", "i": "chat", "n": "still out of scope - weather has no intent_router rule at all, in any script. Not touched in Tier 8; see Readme.MD."}
{"t": "पीसी लॉक मत करो", "i": "chat", "n": "Tier 8: correctly 'chat', for two independent reasons now that lock_pc has Devanagari coverage - (1) the phrase added for lock_pc is the verb-phrase 'कंप्यूटर लॉक करो'/'पीसी लॉक करो' (ending in करो), which never appears as a contiguous substring once 'मत' is inserted before करो, so it simply doesn't match in the first place; (2) even if some future lock phrase did match as a plain substring, _has_standalone_negator() now catches standalone 'मत' as its own word regardless of position (leading or trailing) and defers to the LLM anyway. Belt and suspenders, deliberately - see that function's own docstring in brain/intent_router.py."}
